# Template directives

```rocci
@if List.is_empty(items) {
    <p>Nothing yet.</p>
} @else {
    <p>{List.len(items).to_str()} items</p>
}
```

The body-opening `{` must be on the same logical header line. Parenthesize
records in headers: `@match ({ status, items }) {`.

| Directive | Contract |
| --- | --- |
| `@let name = expr` | Bind before render-producing items. Expression ends at a depth-zero newline. |
| `@if cond { } @else if { } @else { }` | Missing else → `Html.empty`. |
| `@for item in items { }` | One lowercase binder. Lowers to `List.map`. |
| `@match value { Pat => … }` | Arm is element, call, fragment, interpolation, or nested directive. Bare text is not an arm; wrap it. Guards and `\|` alternatives are Roc. |

**Invalid:** markup inside arbitrary Roc expressions; unparenthesized record
headers; `@fixture` inside a component body.

